        "summary": {
            "title": "What you've learned",
            "points": [
                {"text": "Each digit is worth a different amount depending on its column. In 670, the 7 is in the tens column, so it is worth 70."},
                {"text": "Digits after the decimal point are worth less than one. The columns are tenths, hundredths, thousandths and so on."},
                {"text": "A longer decimal is not always bigger. 0.8 is the same as 0.80, so 0.8 is bigger than 0.75."},
                {"text": "Multiplying by 10 moves every digit one column to the left. Dividing by 10 moves every digit one column to the right."},
                {"text": "If you divide one number by 10 and multiply the other by 10, the answer stays the same. 384 × 2 and 38.4 × 20 both make 768."}
            ]
        }
